# Remaining arpeggiator qualification

The arpeggiator implementation and automated checks are complete. Configuration,
controls and runtime limits are in [the user guide](../doc/arpeggiator.md).
Physical timing and receiver qualification remain outstanding.

## Physical qualification

- In poly mode, verify one-press On with a stopped internal clock, held-chord
  capture, chord edits and Off restoring held notes. Listen for stuck or doubled
  notes, including keys already sounding when the effect is enabled.
- In mono mode, record and finish a phrase using the page controls. Check legato,
  repeated pitches, an unfinished final note, release velocity and recorded
  expression. Listen to reordered gestures and verify that cancelling or
  overflowing a new take leaves the committed phrase usable.
- Compare generated attacks and releases with the tapped beat using an
  independently timestamped MIDI receiver. Change tempo mid-step and exercise
  external Start, Continue, Stop and clock dropout at the last measured tempo.
- Block or disconnect one destination while a note sounds or a release is
  pending. Verify cleanup, restoration and progress on healthy destinations,
  without replaying stale attacks after recovery.
- Operate the logical controls and navigate between pages during playback.
  Check display state against the audible and captured MIDI output.

Record receiver captures, timing and practical limits in the target's existing
directory. Host tests do not establish physical timing or musical acceptance.

